0..88 Comment "// Two processes run one program, each migration to `far` in the process it is bound to."
89..91 Comment "//"
92..168 Comment "// It witnesses the world bindings: a world names a process only through the"
169..208 Comment "// host\'s binding, never in the source."
209..211 Comment "//"
212..286 Comment "// One process hosts `far` with `gandr host`, and another runs `main` with"
287..362 Comment "// `gandr run`. Each is given the binding `--world far=<key>@<ip:port>`, or"
363..438 Comment "// the site and the manifold it desugars from. The first migration holds 42"
439..514 Comment "// at `far`. The second reads it there again, a capture the hosting process"
515..590 Comment "// already holds, so nothing is fetched. With no `--world` and no manifold,"
591..650 Comment "// both migrations run in this process and answer the same."
651..653 Comment "//"
654..722 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs` — the two processes"
723..789 Comment "// - see: `two-processes.site.gandr` — the site that hosts `far`"
790..867 Comment "// - see: `two-processes.manifold.gandr` — the manifold placing `far` there"
868..931 Comment "// - see: `twice.gandr` — the same migrations, in one process"
932..1005 Comment "// - see: `corpus/pathological/worlds/open.gandr` — a thunk that cannot"
1006..1016 Comment "//   cross"
